# <%= current_page.data.title %>

This guide helps Integration Hub team members set up their development tools.

## Before you start

- Make sure you have access to the GitHub repository you'll be working on.
- Clone the repository and open it in your preferred editor.
- Follow its README for required tools, dependencies, and local setup.
- Run the documented local checks to confirm your environment is ready.

Requirements vary between projects. For this documentation site, follow the
[local development instructions](https://github.com/ministryofjustice/integration-hub#local-development).

## AI toolkit

We use the Integration Hub AI toolkit to keep AI-assisted contributions
consistent with our engineering standards. Follow the steps below to set it up.

### 1. Install APM

Follow the [APM installation guide](https://microsoft.github.io/apm/getting-started/installation/),
then verify:

```sh
apm --version
```

### 2. Install the toolkit

From a terminal at the root of the
[Integration Hub repository](https://github.com/ministryofjustice/integration-hub),
install the dependencies declared in `apm.yml`:

```sh
apm install --target copilot
```

The currently pinned toolkit supports GitHub Copilot only. Other agents require
additional target support in the upstream toolkit.

If your agent is not following the toolkit guidance, check that you
installed it for the correct target and that the agent has loaded the
instructions.

### Keep the toolkit current

Before starting work in this repository, and again before submitting or updating
a pull request, run:

```sh
apm update
```

This applies whether you make the changes yourself or use an AI agent. If the
instructions change, read the updated guidance, ensure your agent loads it, and
check your work against it before submitting.

Review and include any resulting `apm.lock.yaml` and `apm.yml` changes in your
pull request. Do not commit generated instructions or edit them locally.
You can propose instruction changes in the [MoJ AI toolkit](https://github.com/ministryofjustice/ai-toolkit) repository. Update the
[`integration-hub` folder](https://github.com/ministryofjustice/ai-toolkit/tree/main/toolkits/integration-hub/engineering),
which contains our team instructions.

## Before opening a pull request

- Run `apm update` and check your changes against any updated toolkit guidance.
- Follow the toolkit guidance and review all AI-generated changes.
- Run the relevant [documentation checks](https://github.com/ministryofjustice/integration-hub#local-development) or
  [file-transfer tests](https://github.com/ministryofjustice/integration-hub/blob/main/tests/file-transfer/README.md). Follow the test guide's
  access requirements before running live AWS tests.
- Explain what changed, why, and how it was checked, including any checks not run.
- Never include secrets or sensitive data in prompts, logs, or pull requests.
